---
schema: nodx/1.0
title: Inline Styles And Components
theme: web
components:
  - name: approval-card
    template: |
      :::note {class="nodx-component nodx-component--approval-card" role="approval"}
      ## {{title}}
      {{children}}
      :::
    style: |
      .nodx-component--approval-card {
        border-left: 5px solid var(--nodx-color-primary);
        background-color: #f0fdfa;
      }
profiles:
  requires:
    - core
    - rich
    - style
---

# Inline Styles And Components

:::style
.status-pill {
  display: inline-block;
  border-radius: 999px;
  padding: 0.05em 0.55em;
  font-weight: 700;
  background: #e0f2fe;
  color: #075985;
}
.status-pill.success {
  background: #dcfce7;
  color: #166534;
}
:::style

Normal text can carry [[small visual emphasis]]{.inline-chip color="var(--nodx-color-primary)" bg="#ccfbf1" radius="999px" pad="2px 8px" weight="700"} without leaving paragraph flow.

Use the `highlight` preset for [[short callouts]]{highlight}, or keep classes outside the attribute block with [[status text]].status-pill.success.

::approval-card {title="Approved by design"}
This component is declared in front matter and keeps its children intact.
::
